& [Implementation]
  + one pure cantor_core module revalidates the complete SWA-01 proposal and exact objective before admitting any plan
  + one through 64 unique contiguous steps retain bounded labels lower-only dependencies exact class-derived capability requests and evidence
  + domain-separated request and proposal digests bind the complete predecessor plan authority evidence unresolved and output state

& [Security]
  + all eight capabilities appear exactly once as not_granted_pending_contract and as explicit denials
  + planning_only and admitted_plan_not_executing prevent plan identity from becoming workspace test mutation publication provider effect or activation authority
  + unknown fields boot or objective substitution malformed causal order capability laundering evidence drift output widening and digest tampering fail closed

& [ProductPosition]
  + SWA-02 supplies a machine-executable bounded work proposal but performs none of the proposed work
  + SWA-03 must separately resolve plan steps to admitted substrate and a resumable lifecycle before capability brokerage or execution
